		hk := h % c.NHeadK''','''		hk := kOf[h]''')
s=s.replace('''// l2NormHeads normalises''','''// kHeadOfV is the reference's head map: v-head h reads q/k-head h % NHeadK.
// Modulo and not divide — `iq1 = iv1 % neq1` in the fused op — so the 48
// value heads interleave over the 16 key heads rather than grouping into
// threes. The two maps agree on 16 of the 48 heads, which is exactly enough
// for a wrong one to look nearly right.
func kHeadOfV(c DeltaNetConfig) []int {
	kOf := make([]int, c.NHeadV)
	for h := range kOf {
		kOf[h] = h % c.NHeadK
	}
	return kOf
}

